# Signup attempts

Auth.js does not create a user until they click the magic link. When
Nodemailer sends a link for an email with no existing user:

1. Upsert `signupAttempts` in the Roth database (email, attempt count, tool, surface).
2. Log `[auth] signup attempt`.
3. Email `REGISTRATION_NOTIFY_EMAIL` (`notifySignupAttempt`). Comma-separated
   list is fine. Unset: skip mail.

Existing users (login magic links) are ignored. `createUser` sets
`completedAt` and still sends `notifyNewRegistration`. Failures never
block the magic-link send.
